Hi Winston,

Thanks for the useful heads up.

I am holding back all production with our client servers running R by 6-12 months to minimize experiencing these issues in production. Thankfully, we spot most of them in advance on test servers with test scripts plus human testing of the apps. I have a similar approach with other systems including databases, desktop GUI tools and other analytics platforms.

So many moving parts... :)

Cheers

On Mon, Apr 24, 2017 at 4:57 PM, Winston Chang <win...@rstudio.com> wrote:
> If devtools::session_info() is reporting that some of your packages were built against an earlier version of R, then you have a config file that is setting your .libPaths() (or R_LIBS_USER) in a way that isn't using separate directories for different versions of R. I would suggest fixing that, or else you'll get bitten again by this problem in the future when you upgrade R to 3.5.0 or above.
